        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ജ്വാല",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജ്വാല — jvāla — \"a flame\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മെഴുകുതിരിയുടെ ജ്വാല കാറ്റിൽ ഇളകി. meḻukutiriyuṭe jvāla kāṟṟil iḷaki. The candle's flame shook in the wind."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A literary and news word; plural ജ്വാലകൾ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ജ്വാല (jvāla) is borrowed from Sanskrit jvālā, \"a flame, a blaze\" (Monier-Williams), from the verb jval, \"to burn brightly\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
