        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: നാശനഷ്ടം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാശനഷ്ടം — nāśanaṣṭaṁ — \"damage; losses\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വെള്ളപ്പൊക്കത്തിൽ ഗ്രാമത്തിന് വലിയ നാശനഷ്ടം ഉണ്ടായി. veḷḷappokkattil grāmattinŭ valiya nāśanaṣṭaṁ uṇṭāyi. The village suffered great damage in the flood."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words that say almost the same, destruction and loss: the whole cost of a disaster."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "നാശനഷ്ടം (nāśanaṣṭaṁ) is built from two Sanskrit words: nāśa, \"destruction, ruin\" (CDIAL 7084), and naṣṭa, \"lost, destroyed\" (Monier-Williams), the source of നഷ്ടം (naṣṭaṁ), \"a loss\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
